Subject: Preserve the next-entity handoff after a successful DXF handler

Derived from LibreCAD/libdxfrw 1.0.1, commit
945f2161a13ee521f66f9c52dcfff998e8ccae99, src/libdxfrw.cpp.
The handler updates nextentity before returning true. A compound condition
then falls through, potentially consuming ENDSEC or another entity's data.
Select the entity before invoking its handler; preserve failure propagation,
unknown-record handling and the outer ENDSEC/ENDBLK checks. This is a generic
parser correction, not a RISC-V workaround. The existing DXF contract and
default static/shared converter checks are unchanged. Downstream-only; no
upstream write. Remove when the adopted official release contains this fix.

